ERFA (Essential Routines for Fundamental Astronomy)

The time and frame routines in Sources/CLibAstronomy/EphemerisTime (dtdb.c,
fw2m.c, ir.c, obl06.c, pfw06.c, pmat06.c, rx.c, rz.c, erfa.h, erfam.h) are an
unmodified subset of ERFA 2.0.1, commit
9915ba38c9365f8b0738269b8c2ac1fdd5f8dee3, https://github.com/liberfa/erfa.
Each file retains its original notice. The AstronomyKit wrapper
(ephemeris_time.c and include/ephemeris_time.h) is separate from the official
routines. The IAU 2000A nutation coefficients and the IAU 2006 adjustment
factors in Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Orientation/Generated/IAU2000ATerms.swift
are generated from nut00a.c and nut06a.c of the same ERFA commit, kept
unmodified in Scripts/orientation-data. The complementary terms of the
equation of the equinoxes in
Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Orientation/Generated/EquinoxComplementaryTerms.swift
are generated from eect00.c of the same commit, kept there unmodified too. The
TDB - TT series in
Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Moon/Generated/TDBTerms.swift is generated from
the dtdb.c above, and Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Moon/EngineTDB.swift and
EngineFrameBias.swift port eraDtdb, eraFw2m, eraRx and eraRz. The ERFA
license follows. The long-term precession pole coefficients in
Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Orientation/Generated/Vondrak2011Terms.swift and the
pole/matrix construction in EnginePrecession.swift derive from eraLtpecl,
eraLtpequ and eraLtp of that same release. The unmodified source files and
published ERFA tests are archived in Scripts/orientation-data/long-term with
SHA-256 hashes and their original 2013-2023 NumFOCUS notices. Analytic rates
and rational derivative qualification are AstronomyKit additions.

The apparent-place kernels in EngineApparentPlace.swift derive from ERFA eraAb and eraLd. Eight unmodified ERFA v2.0.1 files, including their published tests and original notices, are archived in Scripts/apparent-place-data. Analytic rates, validation and the TT light-time solver are AstronomyKit additions.

