Native numerical measurement tools

Scripts/solar-numerics/reference.py and solar_reference.py evaluate the NASA Espenak-Meeus Delta T polynomials, IAU Earth Rotation Angle, IAU 2006 precession and mean sidereal time, IAU 2006/2000A nutation with the generated ERFA-derived coefficient and full complementary-term tables, the IERS observer ellipsoid, and VSOP87B with the existing native generated table. The data retain the source attribution and licenses above. The Python evaluator is AstronomyKit-authored and is not software provided by or endorsed by NASA, SOFA, ERFA or IMCCE.

The tools require mpmath 1.3.0, by Fredrik Johansson and contributors, under its BSD license: https://github.com/mpmath/mpmath/blob/1.3.0/LICENSE. mpmath is installed separately for development and is not distributed with the AstronomyKit library.

