NASA/JPL DE441 derived Moon and Pluto tables

Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Moon/Generated/DE441Full holds the Moon's geocentric coefficients, each stored as the binary64 difference of the DE441 Moon and Earth coefficients relative to the Earth-Moon barycenter (targets 301 and 399 relative to target 3), obtained from https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/ftp/eph/planets/bsp/de441.bsp. All coefficients are retained without truncation or quantization. Scripts/moon-data/de441-full-evidence.json, de441-full-component-evidence.json and de441-full-storage-evidence.json record the official source identity, retrieved byte-range SHA-256 hashes, composition bounds and derived payload digests.

The shared-node tables in Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Gravity/Generated/DE441 hold the Pluto system barycenter and the Sun from the same DE441 kernel. Scripts/pluto-data/de441-evidence.json records the same kinds of identity, hash and digest evidence. These are AstronomyKit's compact representations.

Neither set is an official JPL SPK kernel. The JPL reference and NAIF attribution/disclaimer link above apply to the source ephemeris data.

