NASA/JPL DE441, JUP365, NEP098 and URA184 derived planet tables

Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Planets/Generated/DE441 holds binary64 SPK coefficients for the Mercury, Venus, Earth-Moon, Mars, Jupiter, Uranus and Neptune barycenters and the Earth, Jupiter, Uranus and Neptune center offsets. The Mercury, Venus, Earth-Moon, Mars, Jupiter and Neptune barycenters and the Earth offset (target 399 relative to target 3) come from DE441 (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/ftp/eph/planets/bsp/de441.bsp). The Jupiter offset (target 599) comes from JUP365 (https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/satellites/jup365.bsp) and the Neptune offset (target 899) from NEP098 part 1 (https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/satellites/nep098_part-1.bsp). The Uranus barycenter and offset (targets 7 and 799) come from URA184 part 3 (https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/satellites/ura184_part-3.bsp); the barycenter in that kernel is from DE442. The DE441 Sun these tables use is the one in Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Planets/Generated/Saturn, described below. Scripts/planet-data/de441-foundation.json records each source's HTTP identity, retrieved byte-range SHA-256 hashes, record layout and payload digests. The JPL reference and NAIF attribution/disclaimer link above apply. These arrays and their evaluator are AstronomyKit-derived representations, not official JPL SPK kernels or the CSPICE toolkit.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NASA/JPL DE441 and SAT441 derived Saturn tables

Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Planets/Generated/Saturn contains DE441 Saturn-system barycenter and Sun coefficients together with SAT441 Saturn-center offsets from https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/satellites/sat441.bsp. Scripts/saturn-data/assessment.json pins the source HTTP identities, retrieved byte-range SHA-256 hashes, segment descriptors and derived payload digests. All coefficients are retained as binary64. The JPL reference and NAIF attribution/disclaimer link above apply. These packed arrays and their evaluator are AstronomyKit-derived representations, not official JPL SPK kernels or the CSPICE toolkit.

