Galilean moon series

Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Bodies/Generated/JupiterMoonSeries.swift holds the leading terms of the L1.2 theory of the Galilean satellites by Lainey, Duriez and Vienne (2006, Astronomy & Astrophysics 456, 783), which IMCCE publishes at https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/satel/galilean/L1/L1.2/. Scripts/generate-jupiter-moon-series.py generates the table from the copy of the series in Astronomy Engine's astronomy.c, and Scripts/jupiter-moon-data/manifest.json binds it to that source; the generator's --published option compares every term with IMCCE's BisL1.2.dat. The table is a truncated AstronomyKit copy, not software provided by IMCCE or the theory's authors, and carries no endorsement by them.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Observer-event reference archives

Scripts/observer-event-data/sources contains numerical observer output retrieved from NASA/JPL Horizons (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/) and the U.S. Naval Observatory's celestial-navigation and one-day rise/set APIs (https://aa.usno.navy.mil/data/api). Every response has an adjacent query recipe and SHA-256 binding. AstronomyKit's derived fixtures and native comparisons are not official JPL or USNO software or an endorsement by either agency. The publisher responses retain their source descriptions and notices.

