NASA JavaScript Solar Eclipse Explorer reference source

Scripts/reference-data/sources/global-solar/nasa-jsex-program.js is an unchanged archive of the JavaScript Solar Eclipse Explorer by Chris O'Byrne and Fred Espenak, published by NASA GSFC in 2007. AstronomyKit uses the archived program only as a replayable third-party reference for the RP1301 G0 evidence. The file retains its original GNU General Public License version 2-or-later notice. The complete GPLv2 text accompanies it at Scripts/reference-data/sources/global-solar/COPYING.GPL-2.0. These GPL terms apply to the archived JSEX program and do not replace AstronomyKit's own LICENSE.

